# Flowmark exclusions.
#
# POLICY: format the whole repository. Exclude only files we have a specific,
# tested reason to leave raw. Each exclusion below states that reason.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The literature archive: verbatim source and archival transcription.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Two independent reasons, both verified rather than assumed:
#
# 1. The *.raw.md files are unedited pdfminer output and serve as byte-level
#    ground truth for checking the model-assisted *.md transcriptions against.
#    Reflowing them voids that guarantee entirely.
#
# 2. The cleaned *.md transcriptions carry heavy inline LaTeX, and flowmark
#    inserts line breaks INSIDE $...$ spans when it rewraps. Measured on
#    2026-08-22: 31 of 339 math spans broken in the Stromquist transcription,
#    101 of 1236 in Caoduro-Sebo, 5 of 433 in the Kingbird capture. A newline
#    mid-formula defeats grep, and searching this archive locally is the entire
#    point of it. Some Markdown math renderers also require inline math to stay
#    on one line.
#
# So the whole archive stays raw. Its README.md is NOT excluded -- it is our own
# prose and is formatted like everything else.
explorations/packing/resources/papers/
explorations/packing/resources/web/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated agent skill files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# These six SKILL.md files carry explicit DO-NOT-EDIT markers and are regenerated
# byte-deterministically by their own tools (`tbd setup --auto`,
# `softschema skill --install`, `flowmark --install-skill`). Formatting them
# would both diverge them from their generators and be silently overwritten on
# the next regeneration.
#
# Exclusion is per generated skill, NOT per skill directory: hand-written skills
# live alongside these and are formatted like all our other prose. Adding a
# generated skill means adding two lines here; adding a hand-written one means
# adding none.
.agents/skills/flowmark/
.agents/skills/softschema/
.agents/skills/tbd/
.claude/skills/flowmark/
.claude/skills/softschema/
.claude/skills/tbd/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated experiment-loop views.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ledger.md is rebuilt byte-for-byte by campaign/ledger.py and drift-checked by
# `ledger.py --check` in explorations/packing/test.sh. Formatting it makes the
# check fail forever: flowmark rewraps the generated text, ledger.py regenerates
# the unwrapped form, and the two never agree. Measured on 2026-08-22 -- the gate
# failed on the first run after the file was formatted.
explorations/packing/campaign/ledger.md

# defects.md is the same case, and was missed when the rule above was written: it is
# rebuilt by tools/render_defects.py and drift-checked by `render_defects.py --check`
# in the same test.sh. flowmark reflows it today -- verified on 2026-08-23 against
# main, where `flowmark --check` reports it would reformat. Any commit touching
# Markdown on a machine with the lefthook pre-commit hook installed would have
# reformatted it and left the gate failing until someone regenerated it.
#
# The gate now enforces this list rather than trusting it: test.sh fails if a file
# carrying the generated-by banner is not named here.
explorations/packing/defects.md
